Description: fast network scanner with an eBPF/AF_XDP engine and CVE correlation
 tcpcat is a network reconnaissance engine written in Go, intended for
 authorized security assessments and network administration.
 .
 Main features are:
   * TCP SYN/connect and UDP port scanning, with ARP or ping-based host
     discovery
   * service and version detection, including TLS details, and OS
     fingerprinting
   * CVE correlation against an embedded offline database, Google OSV or
     the Vulners API
   * JSON, SARIF, JSONL audit log and baseline-comparison reports
   * scope file and a conservative "safe-production" profile for approved
     engagements
   * optional eBPF/AF_XDP engine on Linux (--ebpf) that only redirects the
     replies to its own probes, leaving all other traffic to the kernel
